              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 410,
                "y": 90,
                "text": "2²ˣ = 2³",
                "size": 34,
                "color": "purple",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 410,
                "y": 170,
                "text": "2x = 3",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "green",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "highlight"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Learn your powers. 1 is a to the 0, and an eighth is 2 to the minus 3.",
          "write": "1 = a⁰,  1/8 = 2⁻³"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Method 2: logarithms",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "5 to the x equals 20. 20 is not a power of 5.",
          "write": "5ˣ = 20"
        },
        {
          "say": "Take logs. x is log 20 divided by log 5.",
          "write": "x = log 20 ÷ log 5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Your calculator gives 1.861, so about 1.86.",
          "write": "x ≈ 1.86"
        },
        {
          "say": "Estimate first. 5 to the 1 is 5, 5 squared is 25. So x is between 1 and 2.",
          "write": "1 < x < 2 ✓"
        },
        {
          "say": "Number you want on top, base on the bottom.",
          "write": "x = log(answer) ÷ log(base)"
        }
      ]
    },
